{
  "//": [
    "Canonical Node resilience dependency fragment (#1145).",
    "",
    "A package.json FRAGMENT, not a package file: merge its `dependencies` and",
    "`devDependencies` blocks into the same package.json you merged the ops-api",
    "payload's package.json.deps into, then `npm install`. The two fragments are",
    "DIFFERENT files -- that one brings the OpenTelemetry packages, this one the",
    "breaker -- and both must be merged. Comments ride in this `//` key, npm's own",
    "convention, so the file stays valid JSON.",
    "",
    "ONE library, deliberately. opossum is the blessed Node circuit breaker; the",
    "bounded jittered retry is a small loop inside dependencyCatalog.ts rather than",
    "a second dependency (README.md, \"Why opossum and no retry library\").",
    "",
    "opossum ships no types, and the strict NodeNext tsconfig rejects an untyped",
    "import, so @types/opossum comes too. Its 8.x line types opossum 10 exactly:",
    "opossum's whole runtime (lib/ and index.js) is byte-identical from 8.5.0",
    "through 9.0.0 to 10.0.0 -- the two majors only narrowed engines.node. The",
    "README's fit-check records the comparison.",
    "",
    "opossum ^10 declares engines.node \"^26 || ^24 || ^22\", which is STRICTER than",
    "the ops-api fragment's OpenTelemetry floor. The two payloads are placed",
    "together or not at all, so this is the pair's joint floor. Under npm's default",
    "engine-strict=false a runtime outside it only WARNS at install -- it installs,",
    "but it is unsupported.",
    "",
    "Your package.json must declare \"type\": \"module\", exactly as for the ops-api",
    "payload: both are NodeNext ESM, and this one reads import.meta.url to find its",
    "declaration file.",
    "",
    "Versions are a floor, not a pin -- Renovate/Dependabot move them."
  ],
  "type": "module",
  "dependencies": {
    "opossum": "^10.0.0"
  },
  "devDependencies": {
    "@types/opossum": "^8.1.9"
  }
}
